# Baked into the production bundle at build time (Vite reads this for
# `npm run build`). Vercel's own environment variables, if set, win over it.
#
# WITHOUT THIS THE DEPLOYED PORTAL CALLS ITSELF. `src/lib/api.ts` falls back
# to the relative '/api/v1' when VITE_API_URL is unset, which works in
# development because the dev server proxies that path to the backend. On
# Vercel there is no proxy, so every request went to
# elizade-web.vercel.app/api/v1 — the portal's own origin, which serves no
# API — and came back as the HTML 404 page.
#
# The value must include /api/v1: it REPLACES the whole base, it is not
# joined to it. (The service board next door uses the opposite convention —
# origin only — because its call sites carry the prefix themselves.)
#
# The backend must also list this app's origin in CORS_ORIGINS, or the
# browser blocks the response before the app ever sees it.
VITE_API_URL=https://elizade-backend-api-production-0daa.up.railway.app/api/v1
